2026-07-10T07:36:29.2984914Z     
2026-07-10T07:36:29.2985196Z     The ``pytest`` framework makes it easy to write small tests, yet
2026-07-10T07:36:29.2985693Z     scales to support complex functional testing for applications and libraries.
2026-07-10T07:36:29.2986086Z     
2026-07-10T07:36:29.2986289Z     An example of a simple test:
2026-07-10T07:36:29.2986536Z     
2026-07-10T07:36:29.2986726Z     .. code-block:: python
2026-07-10T07:36:29.2986950Z     
2026-07-10T07:36:29.2987142Z         # content of test_sample.py
2026-07-10T07:36:29.2987409Z         def inc(x):
2026-07-10T07:36:29.2987618Z             return x + 1
2026-07-10T07:36:29.2987834Z     
2026-07-10T07:36:29.2988004Z     
2026-07-10T07:36:29.2988196Z         def test_answer():
2026-07-10T07:36:29.2988430Z             assert inc(3) == 5
2026-07-10T07:36:29.2988657Z     
2026-07-10T07:36:29.2988833Z     
2026-07-10T07:36:29.2989010Z     To execute it::
2026-07-10T07:36:29.2989208Z     
2026-07-10T07:36:29.2989383Z         $ pytest
2026-07-10T07:36:29.2989823Z         ============================= test session starts =============================
2026-07-10T07:36:29.2990398Z         collected 1 items
2026-07-10T07:36:29.2990634Z     
2026-07-10T07:36:29.2998284Z         test_sample.py F
2026-07-10T07:36:29.2998555Z     
2026-07-10T07:36:29.2998827Z         ================================== FAILURES ===================================
2026-07-10T07:36:29.2999010Z         _________________________________ test_answer _________________________________
2026-07-10T07:36:29.2999090Z     
2026-07-10T07:36:29.2999193Z             def test_answer():
2026-07-10T07:36:29.2999288Z         >       assert inc(3) == 5
2026-07-10T07:36:29.2999383Z         E       assert 4 == 5
2026-07-10T07:36:29.2999483Z         E        +  where 4 = inc(3)
2026-07-10T07:36:29.2999556Z     
2026-07-10T07:36:29.2999673Z         test_sample.py:5: AssertionError
2026-07-10T07:36:29.2999836Z         ========================== 1 failed in 0.04 seconds ===========================
2026-07-10T07:36:29.2999924Z     
2026-07-10T07:36:29.3000003Z     
2026-07-10T07:36:29.3001089Z     Thanks to ``pytest``'s detailed assertion introspection, you can simply use plain ``assert`` statements. See `getting-started <https://docs.pytest.org/en/stable/getting-started.html#our-first-test-run>`_ for more examples.
2026-07-10T07:36:29.3001182Z     
2026-07-10T07:36:29.3001265Z     
2026-07-10T07:36:29.3001356Z     Features
2026-07-10T07:36:29.3001438Z     --------
2026-07-10T07:36:29.3001521Z     
2026-07-10T07:36:29.3002003Z     - Detailed info on failing `assert statements <https://docs.pytest.org/en/stable/how-to/assert.html>`_ (no need to remember ``self.assert*`` names)
2026-07-10T07:36:29.3002086Z     
2026-07-10T07:36:29.3002183Z     - `Auto-discovery
2026-07-10T07:36:29.3002475Z       <https://docs.pytest.org/en/stable/explanation/goodpractices.html#python-test-discovery>`_
2026-07-10T07:36:29.3002581Z       of test modules and functions
2026-07-10T07:36:29.3002659Z     
2026-07-10T07:36:29.3002930Z     - `Modular fixtures <https://docs.pytest.org/en/stable/explanation/fixtures.html>`_ for
2026-07-10T07:36:29.3003104Z       managing small or parametrized long-lived test resources
2026-07-10T07:36:29.3003183Z     
2026-07-10T07:36:29.3003439Z     - Can run `unittest <https://docs.pytest.org/en/stable/how-to/unittest.html>`_ (or trial)
2026-07-10T07:36:29.3003542Z       test suites out of the box
2026-07-10T07:36:29.3003621Z     
2026-07-10T07:36:29.3003713Z     - Python 3.10+ or PyPy3
2026-07-10T07:36:29.3003791Z     
2026-07-10T07:36:29.3004268Z     - Rich plugin architecture, with over 1300+ `external plugins <https://docs.pytest.org/en/latest/reference/plugin_list.html>`_ and thriving community
2026-07-10T07:36:29.3004341Z     
